              "description": {
                "type": "textComponent",
                "text": "The first ever NCAA Men's Ice Hockey played on Martha's Vineyard Island is broadcast exclusively via Martha's Vineyard Public Broadcasting Station!"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Martha's Vineyard Football",
          "subtitle": "undefined · 8 yrs 5 mos",
          "breakdown": true,
          "subComponents": [
            {
              "title": "Official Videographer",
              "caption": "Sep 2013 - Feb 2022 · 8 yrs 5 mos",
              "metadata": "Martha's Vineyard Regional High School",
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "All things must pass, it seems.  With the retirement from broadcasting after 40 illustrious years of Mr. Ken Goldberg, and the reretirement of our legendary Hall of Fame Coach Donald Herman, it is time for me to step down as the Official Videographer of the Martha’s Vineyard Regional High School Football Team after nine glorious Seasons.  My Great Uncle Dan McCarthy founded the MVRHS program in 1960, and it has been my distinct privilege, and proud honor to continue in his tradition, and serve the Island community to the best of my ability through these years.  All of this work is archived with MVTV in perpetuity.\n   I’m definitely going to miss being high above the 50 yard line with the best vista in the stadium, and I hope I am remembered fondly for my commitment to the Team.  Thanks for the memories, and Go Vineyarders!"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Official Videographer",
              "caption": "Dec 2013 - Dec 2018 · 5 yrs",
              "metadata": "Martha's Vineyard Regional High School",
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "Five fabulous seasons above center ice proudly continuing my family's tradition in the Martha's Vineyard community.  All games aired on television, and the web via MVTV."
                }
              ]
            }
